  "description": "The Brief's Adverse Conditions rows under its findings, the standard briefing's first element (AIM 7-1-5(b)(1)): what the flight meets on the route while it is there (OnRoute `when` \"during\", or none given) -- a TFR the route goes through (14 CFR 91.137-91.145) and a Convective SIGMET or SIGMET (AIM 7-1-6), stops; a Center Weather Advisory (AIM 7-1-6), an urgent pilot report (UUA, AIM 7-1-18) and an AIRMET or G-AIRMET (AIM 7-1-6), cautions -- in that order, of a kind the one met first along the route first, at most three, with how many more. A TFR only near the route, a routine PIREP and a hazard before or after the flight are left to their pages. Each row's time is for the host to write: `at` when the flight meets a TFR, `until` an advisory's end, `reported` a pilot report's time.",
